  "aiReview": {
    "strengths": {
      "bestArea": "Catch-and-shoot three-point shooting on real volume — 40.6% FG on 106 three-point attempts (Excellent, 91st percentile), climbing to 61.9% when left unguarded. Also a very efficient finisher at the rim (80.0% FG, Excellent, 99th percentile) and off the dribble (42.1% FG on the dribble jumper, Excellent).",
      "bestPlayType": "Spot Up — his largest role by far (51.7% of possessions, 74 on the season) and Excellent-graded (1.189 PPP, 90th percentile). Transition is a close second (1.290 PPP, Very Good) and even better per-possession.",
      "overallStrength": "An efficient, high-volume shooter for a big man — nearly every shot type and shot distance category graded Good or better, and his two highest-usage play types (Spot Up, Transition) are also his best-graded. For someone used primarily off spot-ups and in transition, that's an ideal alignment of volume and efficiency."
    },
    "weaknesses": {
      "worstArea": "Nothing stands out at real volume the way Off Screen does among his play types (see below) — his shot profile is efficient across the board.",
      "worstPlayType": "Off Screen — graded Poor (7th percentile, 0.533 PPP) on real volume (15 possessions, 10.5% of his offense), a clear outlier next to his Spot Up and Transition efficiency.",
      "overallWeakness": "The one action that doesn't fit his otherwise efficient profile is coming off screens — a real gap given how good he is on nearly everything else, including catch-and-shoot jumpers off other actions.",
      "developmentTarget": "Work on using screens/movement more effectively — given how well he shoots when set (Spot Up) or in space (Transition), the Off Screen inefficiency looks more like a timing/reads issue than a shooting problem worth addressing on film."
    }
